<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-china"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20China.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of China</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">UN Resolution 2758 transfers China’s seat to the People’s Republic</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/peoples-republic-of-china"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/People's%20Republic%20of%20China.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>People's Republic of China</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The People’s Republic takes China’s seat at the United Nations</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/swiss-confederation"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Swiss%20Confederation.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Swiss Confederation</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Women gain the right to vote in federal elections</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/sheikhdom-of-sharjah"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Sheikhdom%20of%20Sharjah.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Sheikhdom of Sharjah</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Sharjah joins the United Arab Emirates on 2 December</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/united-arab-emirates"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/United%20Arab%20Emirates.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>United Arab Emirates</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Six sheikhdoms proclaim the United Arab Emirates on 2 December</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-india"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20India.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of India</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">India's victory in the Bangladesh Liberation War creates Bangladesh</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/uganda"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Uganda.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Uganda</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Idi Amin seizes power in a military coup</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/language/old-norse"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Old%20Norse.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Old Norse</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Denmark returns the Codex Regius and Flateyjarbók to Iceland, the first of the medieval manuscripts to go home</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/womens-suffrage-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Women's%20suffrage%20movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Women's suffrage movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Swiss men vote to give women the vote in federal elections</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/islamic-republic-of-pakistan"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Islamic%20Republic%20of%20Pakistan.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Islamic Republic of Pakistan</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">After the military refuses to transfer power to the Awami League and launches Operation Searchlight, war with India ends in defeat and East Pakistan becomes Bangladesh.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/singapore"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Singapore.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Singapore</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Britain withdraws its forces in October, leaving a token British, Australian and New Zealand presence; the Singapore Armed Forces, built with Israeli instructors, must guarantee independence.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-bhutan"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Bhutan.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Bhutan</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Bhutan is admitted to the United Nations after three years as an observer and is the first country to recognise Bangladesh's independence.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/inuit"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Inuit.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Inuit</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Inuit found the Inuit Tapirisat of Canada, today Inuit Tapiriit Kanatami</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/religion/mithraism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Mithraism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Mithraism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">At the First International Congress of Mithraic Studies, John R. Hinnells and R. L. Gordon severely criticise Cumont’s theory of Persian origins</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/cyrus-cylinder"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Cyrus%20Cylinder.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Cyrus Cylinder</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Cylinder was displayed in Tehran for the celebration of 2,500 years of Persian monarchy</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/american-indian-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/American%20Indian%20Movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>American Indian Movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Members occupy Mount Rushmore for a few days to protest the seizure of the Black Hills, and briefly occupy the headquarters of the Bureau of Indian Affairs in Washington</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/liberation-theology"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Liberation%20theology.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Liberation theology</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Peruvian priest Gustavo Gutiérrez coins the term and writes A Theology of Liberation</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/utilitarianism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Utilitarianism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Utilitarianism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">John Rawls's A Theory of Justice brings to prominence the objection that utilitarianism ignores the distinction between persons</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/libertarianism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Libertarianism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Libertarianism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A small group led by David Nolan forms the Libertarian Party</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/secularism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Secularism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Secularism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">John Rawls publishes A Theory of Justice, whose line of work leads many political theorists to prefer overlapping consensus to secularism</span></li></ul></section>
